---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TerminalPanel from '../components/TerminalPanel.astro';
import { releaseNote } from '../data/release';
---
<Base description="A small macOS menu bar app that picks today's Spotify playlist for the genre you like and the mood you are coding in.">
  <TerminalPanel slot="masthead" />
  <h1>Sudo Play</h1>
  <p class="lead">A small macOS menu bar app that picks today's Spotify playlist, based on what you are coding and how you feel about it.</p>
  <figure class="window">
    <picture>
      <source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="/screenshots/window-dark.webp" />
      <img src="/screenshots/window-light.webp" width="360" height="520" alt="The Sudo Play window. Jazz and Coffee Needed are selected, and today's pick is Jazz for deep work, with Play, Next and Surprise me below." />
    </picture>
  </figure>
  <p>Pick a genre, like rock or Lo-fi. Pick a developer mood, like Friday Deploy or Debugging. Press Play, and the playlist opens in Spotify.</p>
  <p>The pick is the same all day, and the same for everyone who chooses the same genre and mood. Tomorrow it changes.</p>
  <p>The line at the top of this page is the tagline, not a command. There is nothing to type in a terminal.</p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>The app has no accounts, no analytics and no tracking. The app downloads one catalog file and opens public playlist links. Nothing about you leaves your Mac.</p>

  <h2>Where to start</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a>: genres, moods and the daily pick.</li>
    <li><a href="/install/">Install</a>: how to get the app onto your Mac. {releaseNote()}</li>
    <li><a href="/moods/">Moods</a>: what each mood is for.</li>
    <li><a href="/tips/">Tips</a>: small ways to get more from the app.</li>
    <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>: what this website loads.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The app window, at its natural size, cropped from a 2x capture without
     the macOS shadow: the site is flat. A hairline gives it an edge on a page
     the same colour as the window. The radius is the window's own. */
  .window {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .window img {
    display: block;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 22px;
    outline: 1px solid var(--border);
    outline-offset: -1px;
  }
</style>
